.Dd August 22, 2026
.Dt MAC_LOMAC_GROK 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mac_lomac_grok
.Nd
.Xr mac_lomac 4
kernel policy as loaded by
.Xr mac_lomac_grok 8
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To load the policy at boot, after
.Xr mac_lomac_grok 8 Cm stage :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
mac_lomac_load="YES"
security.mac.lomac.enabled=0
security.mac.lomac.trust_all_interfaces=1
security.mac.lomac.ptys_equal=1
.Ed
.Pp
Enforcement is off until
.Nm mac_lomac_grok Cm enforce .
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This page documents the
.Em configured
kernel interface.
The implementation is
.Xr mac_lomac 4
in
.Pa /boot/kernel/mac_lomac.ko
.Pq GENERIC includes options MAC .
.Pp
.Xr mac_lomac 4
is an integrity (low-watermark) policy: a subject that reads a
lower-grade object is demoted and then cannot write higher-grade
objects.
.Dq equal
is exempt from those comparisons.
.Ss Sysctl
See
.Xr mac_lomac 4 .
This package sets:
.Bl -tag -width security.mac.lomac.trust_all_interfaces
.It Va security.mac.lomac.enabled
0 until
.Cm enforce ;
.Cm unenforce
or
.Cm uninstall
returns it to 0.
.It Va security.mac.lomac.trust_all_interfaces
Loader tunable
.Pq RDTUN .
Must appear in
.Xr loader.conf 5
so interfaces are not
.Dq low
.Pq which would demote SSH .
.It Va security.mac.lomac.ptys_equal
Label new ptys
.Dq equal .
.El
.Ss Labels
File labels come from
.Xr setfsmac 8
using the official PLM sample
.Pa /usr/share/security/lomac-policy.contexts ,
the Xorg overlay
.Pa x11-xorg.contexts ,
and an optional site overlay.
Subject labels come from
.Xr login.conf 5
.Va label
on login classes
.Dq trusted
.Pq high(low-high)
and
.Dq sandbox
.Pq 10[2] ,
with
.Dq root
.Dq equal(equal-equal)
unless
.Pa POLICY
overrides them.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mac_lomac 4 ,
.Xr mac 4 ,
.Xr maclabel 7 ,
.Xr mac_lomac_grok 8 ,
.Xr mac_lomac_grok 7 ,
.Xr setfsmac 8
.Sh BUGS
ZFS has no
.Xr tunefs 8
.Cm multilabel
flag.
.Nm mac_lomac_grok Cm label
probes
.Xr setfmac 8
on
.Pa /tmp
and aborts if file labels are unsupported.
.Pp
.Xr setfsmac 8
applies only the first matching spec entry; the official PLM lists
.Pa /dev(/.*)?
equal before later
.Pa /dev
high lines, so this package feeds overlay specfiles first.
.Pp
.Xr mac_lomac 4
may revoke
.Xr mmap 2
on demotion.
Handbook ch.19
.Pq troubleshooting: sticky UFS multilabel, Xorg, _secure_path, whoami/root
and mailing-list/PR notes
.Pq USENIX trusted binaries vs FreeBSD labels, PR 178667 aux/extattr, /dev PLM vs DRM/evdev
are catalogued in the package
.Pa README
section
.Dq Known issues .

